course: dictionary
lesson: 12271
title: Continuation: carrying on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A continuation is the next part that carries on from something that came before. The word comes from continue, which means to keep going. «Maya's story ended on a cliffhanger, so she wrote a continuation the next day.» The continuation picks up exactly where the first part stopped.
explain: Continuation can also mean the act of carrying on without stopping. «The team's continuation of the project meant they never took a break.» The team kept going and did not stop. Look for clue words like next, after, carries on and without stopping.
explain: Continuation is a noun, so it names a thing or an action. You can find it in many subjects. In maths, the continuation of a pattern is the numbers that come next. In history, the continuation of a tradition is the way it keeps going through the years. Check your meaning by swapping in carrying on, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A continuation is something that carries on from something before.
fact: Continuation is a noun: one continuation, many continuations.
fact: Continuation can mean the act of carrying on without stopping.
fact: In maths, the continuation of the pattern 2, 4, 6, 8 is 10, 12, 14.
fact: The word comes from «continue», which means to keep going.
exercise: «The story ended on a cliffhanger, so Maya wrote a continuation the next day.» What is a continuation here? | A picture drawn on the cover | *The next part of the story, carrying on from the cliffhanger | A reason to stop reading
exercise: «The number pattern was 2, 4, 6, 8.» What is its continuation? | 1, 3, 5, 7 | 8, 6, 4, 2 | *10, 12, 14
exercise: «The village kept a continuation of its old harvest dance.» What does continuation mean here? | *Carrying on the tradition without stopping | A brand new dance invented today | Stopping the dance for ever
test: «The team's continuation of the project meant they never took a break.» What does continuation mean here? | Stopping for a long holiday | *Carrying on without stopping | Making a cake for the team
test: Which word is the root of continuation, the word it comes from? | contest | *continue | continent
exam: Mr Okafor says, «The continuation of the lesson is on page nine.» What does he mean? | *The next part, carrying on from where we stopped | The lesson is over and everyone can go home | A page nobody needs to read
